WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.042
Retail devices are physical items owned by your shop.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:07.667
Start by choosing new or refurbished at the top.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:12.083
Never create a retail record for a customer's repair device.

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:18.375
Enter the category, brand and model, then copy identifiers from
the physical device.

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:22.625
Two devices of the same model still need separate records.

00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:28.250
Record memory, built-in storage and individual drives
separately where applicable.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.792
Leave unknown values empty, not zero.

00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:36.292
Do not infer this device's configuration from its product name.

00:00:36.292 --> 00:00:40.875
Check condition, battery and accessories on the same page.

00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:43.958
Photos can be saved with the new record.

00:00:43.958 --> 00:00:47.833
Never mark checks complete unless they were performed.

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:51.917
The default only creates a record for later inspection.

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:59.875
If all three checks are complete, enter a valid asking price
and explicitly choose to create and make available in one save.

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:03.292
Open the sale form from product details.

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:08.083
Enter the buyer, actual payments and delivery in the same form.

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:11.667
Check the warranty and confirm the sale once.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:17.875
Print after saving; later payments and after-sales cases remain
linked to the original sale.
